/*
  Localizable.strings (Ukrainian)
  Shared (App)

  Hand-synced, key for key, with `apps/safari-host-app/src/i18n/messages-uk.ts`.
  A key omitted here falls back to `en.lproj/Localizable.strings`, so an
  untranslated string degrades to English rather than to a raw key.

  Two wording notes carried over from the TS catalogue, both of which look like
  copy-paste slips and are not:

  - `chips.settings` and `chips.settingsLegacy` are the SAME word. The
    Settings/Preferences split is an English-only rename; Apple's Ukrainian
    wording did not change with macOS 13. Same for `openPreferences.label`
    and `openPreferences.legacy`.
  - Apple's app is «Параметри»; Movar's own settings tab stays «Налаштування»
    (`tabs.settings`). That is our UI, not Apple's, and conflating them would
    send the reader to the wrong screen.
*/

